    description: "The other half of the owner's 2026-09-01 ruling (a) on WI-livar, scoped with\nINV-tafig. This is the module-key axis itself: ADR-0024 steps 1-4, PHASE 1 ONLY.\n\nTHE DECLARATION THAT EXISTS TODAY IS FALSE, AND RETIRING IT IS PART OF THE WORK.\nir.py:743 reads:\n\n    module_path: str  # axis: free-text -- module import path in source-language\n    grammar; consumers display/lookup, never branch on the value itself.\n\nA consumer branches on the value itself. io_boundary.py:3644 _module_matches\ndecides type-vs-sub-package from ORTHOGRAPHY (longer_raw[shared][:1].isupper())\nand its Swift carve-out branches on the value being a single token the catalogue\nname ends with. The linter passes the declaration because a free-text\njustification must be PRESENT, not TRUE. So this item does not only add an axis,\nit removes a wrong one -- and the false justification is the reason the gap\nsurvived a linter that was already running over this exact line.\n\nSHAPE: STRUCTURAL POLICY, NOT AN ENUMERABLE VALUE SET. Module names cannot be\nenumerated, so this follows qualified_name_axis.py -- a module-level declaration\nplus accessors, no per-value Spec dataclass -- under ADR-0024 section 4's \"use\njudgment\" carveout, NOT the heavyweight edge_types.py shape that the sibling\nio-boundary axis takes. State that choice and its precedent in the ADR; a\nreviewer will otherwise ask why the two siblings differ.\n\nWHAT THE AXIS DECLARES is the DISCRIMINATOR _module_matches currently guesses:\nwhich NOTION the slot carries on a given row. The audit measured six over 65,187\nexternal refs on a 21-repo cold cohort -- namespace, TYPE, global-object VALUE,\nreceiver-VARIABLE name, DISJUNCTION (cpp's comma-joined include set), and\nSENTINEL -- with 7.8% not a single module identity. Objective-C writes\nmodule_path=receiver_name literally; 1,102 of 4,207 refs (26%) on the objc+swift\nrepos carry a local identifier. Write-up:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-module-key_09012026.md\n\nDELIVERABLES: the ADR (axiom + the six notions + why structural-policy); the\nregistry module with its accessor; the axis wired into\nmulti_value_field_axis._known_axes(); the ir.py:743 declaration changed from the\nfalse free-text to the new axis; a property test. The drift-linter shape is\nshared with the io-boundary sibling -- reuse it, do not write a second one.\n\nEXPLICITLY OUT OF SCOPE, and this is the boundary that keeps the item unblocked:\nchanging what analyzers PUT in the slot. external_symbol ids embed the module\nslot (rust:external:0-0:File::open), so a value migration changes emitted ids and\nneeds a scheme bump, which WI-talos DECISION 3 gates behind v9/v10 and two\nreleases. That is ADR-0024 step 7 and is filed separately. Declaring the axis is\nadditive and ships now."  # f0ec
    fields: {}  # f0ec
